mport settings; print(settings.execution_runner_url)\"` after adding the config key.\n\nReturn a summary of every change you make (file, line, what changed).","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:33.114Z","userPrompt":"Fix 3 critical bugs in the nexi package. Read the files first, then apply edits.\n\n**Bug 1: nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py**\n- Line 56: `pattern_store.get_failing_patterns()` doesn't exist. The correct method is `await pattern_store.fetch_low_success(max_success_rate=0.4, min_confidence=0.5)`. The `check_and_queue` method must become async.\n- Lines 75-77, 113-115: Queries `consolidation_jobs` and `extractor_runs` tables that don't exist. Replace with queries against `system_state` table:\n  - Rule 2: `SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_consolidation_run'`\n  - Rule 4: `SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_extraction_run'`\n- Line 93: Health check URL is `http://i9-node:8080/health` but the service exposes port 8000. Read from config: `settings.vllm_health_url` with default `http://vllm-gemma4:8000/health`. Also wire `_http` in the factory (check how it's initialized).\n\n**Bug 2: nexi/nexi/main.py**\n- Line 201: `settings.xnch_base_url.replace(\"8001\", \"8001\")` is a no-op (replaces 8001 with 8001). Change to use a config key or stopgap: add `execution_runner_url: str = \"http://localhost:8002\"` to nexi/nexi/config.py, then use `settings.execution_runner_url` in main.py. Read nexi/nexi/config.py first to see the Settings class.\n\nVerify: Run `cd /Users/xnch/xnchSystems && .venv/bin/python -c \"from nexi.nexi.config import settings; print(settings.execution_runner_url)\"` after adding the config key.\n\nReturn a summary of every change you make (file, line, what changed)."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p5s8_903d504da189":{"observation":{"hookType":"config_loaded","id":"obs_mqv8p5s8_903d504da189","raw":{"agents":["languages/python-pro","ai/data-engineer","ai/data-scientist